zoe: Quick design pass on 'shadow + weave' dark theme for the console. Two quick issues: sparklines vanish in card shadows, and the compact heatmap squares are indistinguishable for several CVD profiles. dropping a small var set and a pattern idea.

mika: paste the vars pls so I can try it in Storybook. :coffee:

zoe: sure — minimal set: ```
--bg: #0b0e11;
--panel: #111316;
--muted: #98a1a7;
--brand: #64c8ff;
--spark: rgba(100,200,255,0.6);
--heat-low: #47b6a4;
--heat-mid: #ffd87a;
--heat-high: #ff7358;
```

otto: spark at 0.6 still disappears when the card gets inset shadow. Can we bump to 0.9 or add a 1px outer glow on hover?

priya: accessibility note: small percentages and legend text are failing 4.5:1 against --panel. For tiny labels either raise contrast or increase font-size/weight. Also ensure focus outlines are visible (3:1 minimum).

mika: heatmap: low/med are too close under deuteranopia. Two options: change hues (teal -> yellow -> warm) or add a pattern overlay for low values. I prefer offering both: color shift + optional patterns.

zoe: updated proposal: bump sparkline alpha to 0.9, swap heatmap to teal/yellow/warm, and add a settings toggle "Heatmap: Color + patterns (accessibility)" with tooltip "Improves readability for color-vision differences." Example updated vars: ```
--spark: rgba(100,200,255,0.9);
--heat-low: #3fb2a3;
--heat-mid: #ffd67f;
--heat-high: #ff775e;
```

otto: legend in compact layout is greedy — collapse to a single icon that expands on hover/focus. Keyboard users should be able to open it with Enter; focus ring must be visible.

priya: agreed. Also add a note in the spec to run automated contrast checks for: small legend labels, inline percentages, and code tokens when adjacent to charts. For code vs charts: consider a subtle inner border on code blocks so code tokens keep brightness without flooding the visual hierarchy.

mika: copy nit: avoid "color-blind mode" label. Use your proposed wording or "Heatmap patterns (accessibility)". Shorter: "Heatmap: Color + patterns" with tooltip as you wrote.

zoe: plan of record:
- sparkline opacity -> 0.9 + subtle hover glow
- heatmap: teal / yellow / warm red + optional hatch overlay when toggle enabled
- collapse legend into hover/focus popover in compact views; ensure keyboard access and visible focus states
- bump small-label contrast or size per a11y checklist; add code-block inner border to separate zones

design-bot: Figma frame uploaded: https://figma.com/file/shadow-weave-compact (zoe/shadow-weave-dark-pass)

zoe: I'll open a small PR with the CSS vars, Storybook fixture (compact dashboard), and a checklist for QA to run color-vision simulators + automated contrast reports. Pinging @priya for the accessibility sign-off once tests land. Thanks! :white_check_mark:
